; ============================================================
;  ARMOR MAG POUCHES - what a corpse must not throw away
;
;  GENERATED by art/mkdrops.py from l_amp_rigs.ltx.
;
;  THE ROLL IS NOT HERE ANY MORE.
;
;    "add mcm subcategory 'rig and pouch drop' and add sliders for rig
;     and mag pouches drops ... per npc rank"
;
;  It used to be: eight ranks by thirteen communities of `section =
;  chance` in the Economy fork's own death tables, which is the right
;  mechanism right up until somebody wants a slider. An ltx is read
;  once at load and cannot be moved from a menu, so the sixty-four
;  chances live in MCM and the roll lives in the script - see A.drop_def
;  and A.on_npc_death.
;
;  WHAT IS LEFT IS ONE LINE PER ITEM. death_manager builds
;  always_keep_item out of [keep_items] and checks it FIRST in
;  keep_item, ahead of everything that releases. Our things are put on
;  the corpse after decide_items_to_keep has already walked it, so this
;  is belt and braces - and it is worth having because the release at
;  the end of keep_item is COMMENTED OUT in the fork we read, and a
;  feature that rests on another mod's commented-out line is a feature
;  that breaks on their release rather than on ours.
;
;  ! IS THE OVERRIDE MARKER. [keep_items] belongs to the Economy fork's
;  death_generic.ltx, and a second PLAIN declaration of a foreign
;  section is a fatal error at startup.
; ============================================================


